{"type":"message","id":"ac3e447f","parentId":"6fcd32d8","timestamp":"2026-05-26T09:29:00.811Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying that a task sent via WeChat (微信) reported an error. Let me look at the WeChat session more closely. From the sessions list, I found the WeChat session for the wxlee agent:\n\n- `agent:wxlee:openclaw-weixin:a23ee0675df2-im-bot:direct:o9cq802uvmveggp0xkfm4o7acdrg@im.wechat`\n\nThe last response (the one about APT packages) seems to have completed successfully - it shows status \"done\" and a `stopReason: \"stop\"`. But the assistant response was very long and detailed.\n\nWait, let me re-read the user's message more carefully. They said \"刚刚微信发给你的任务你报错了\" - \"The task I sent you via WeChat just now reported an error.\" \n\nAnd looking at the session transcript, the last message at the bottom shows `stopReason: \"error\"` at one point (timed out), and then a second error after that too. But it eventually finished. The user might be referring to something else though - perhaps the error messages (`stopReason: \"error\"` with \"request timed out\") that occurred during processing.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the transcript:\n- Line ~26 area: `stopReason: \"error\"`, `errorMessage: \"request timed out\"` - the assistant timed out\n- Then it continued and eventually produced the full response with `stopReason: \"stop\"` \n\nSo the session had some timeout errors during processing, but it seems like the final response was delivered. Let me look at what happened on the WeChat side - maybe the message wasn't delivered properly or the error was visible on the WeChat end.\n\nLet me check the logs more thoroughly for errors related to this session.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bbd4b0f969844b3b9a010e65","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"99e5eec8\\|1779772763873\\|weixin.*177977276\" /home/node/.openclaw/logs/ 2>/dev/null | tail -2