{"type":"message","id":"9c73fcfd","parentId":"41c76aed","timestamp":"2026-05-26T13:05:31.069Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user asked \"怎么回事\" (What's going on?) after receiving my previous message. They seem confused - likely they don't understand who I am or why I'm addressing them as \"主公\". Looking at the context:\n\n1. This is a direct message on Feishu from user `ou_9e18438fb941decf11a0b88d78fe2b50`\n2. I'm the `wxlee` agent (小夜/军师 persona)\n3. The user's first message was just \"嗨\" (Hi), then they asked about a WeChat task error\n4. I've been using \"主公\" addressing and a \"军师\" (strategist) persona\n\nThe user might not be Lucifer (the actual owner / \"主公\"). They might be another person who reached out asking about the WeChat task error on behalf of Lucifer. The ID `ou_9e18438fb941decf11a0b88d78fe2b50` is different from the authorized senders listed in my system prompt (`ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff`, `ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a`).\n\nLooking at the first message again - it was \"嗨\" and then they said \"刚刚微信发给你的任务你报错了，查一查\" - \"The task we just sent you via WeChat reported an error, check it.\" This is likely a colleague or someone working with Lucifer who knows about the WeChat task.\n\nThe user seems confused by my \"主公\" address. They're asking \"怎么回事\" (What's going on?/What's this about?).\n\nI should clarify - apologize for the confusion, explain who I am, and ask who they are. I should not assume they're the \"主公\" (Lucifer).","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"抱歉，看来我的称呼让您困惑了。\n\n我默认用了\"主公\"的称谓，是因为这个助手账号平时为 Lucifer 服务，预设了军师角色。您第一次发消息来说微信任务报错，我以为是您通过其他通道给我派的任务。\n\n请问您是 Lucifer 本人，还是他的朋友/同事？我需要知道怎么称呼您，免得再闹误会。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop"